fter playing RedJoker, we’d be left with weak singles. Still, taking control now might allow us to play ♦J or ♣4 next turn, possibly helping our teammate gain the lead.\n\nAlternatively, if we pass, the landlord continues unimpeded — possibly playing another high card or bomb. Since our teammate passed, they likely couldn’t beat ♣2 either, meaning neither peasant had a 2 or joker until us. That makes our RedJoker the only available counter in the peasant team.\n\nThus, **now is the right time to play RedJoker** — it beats the landlord’s play, seizes control, and may open a window for our teammate to unload low cards.\n\nReason: The only way to beat ♣2 is with RedJoker (rocket isn\'t possible, only one joker). Not playing it means letting the landlord maintain control with no resistance. Given that both teammates have limited power, using RedJoker now to seize initiative is optimal, even at the cost of losing a high card early. It forces the landlord out and allows us to lead with a low card next turn, potentially helping our teammate progress.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["RedJoker"]}'}
